# Bun 1.4.3 — corresponding source

This document records where the source corresponding to the packaged Bun
candidate came from. It is a factual reference list. It is **not** a statement
that the corresponding-source obligation is satisfied: this package ships the
upstream binary and its notices, not the source archives.

## Corresponding upstream source

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Release tag | `bun-v1.4.3` |
| Bun source commit | `c6da4a4d3010e5553438c60f6bd76d981976867c` |
| WebKit / JavaScriptCore commit | `0c06faadf65bf8e8c8ad3a5a8aca83e1e9ed653f` |
| TinyCC commit | `05f0fafaa3be31e31d7b4b5c17dc60f62c991171` |

Source tree:
<https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/tree/bun-v1.4.3>

Every reference above is pinned to an exact tag or commit, never to `main` or
to a branch head.

## Pinned build patch

Bun builds its vendored TinyCC with this reviewed patch applied:

<https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/bun-v1.4.3/patches/tinycc/tcc.h.patch>

## Rebuilding from source

Upstream documents its own local build in the source tree. In short:

1. Clone `oven-sh/bun` at tag `bun-v1.4.3`.
2. Check out `oven-sh/WebKit` at the commit above into `vendor/WebKit` (upstream
   provides `bun sync-webkit-source` to do this at the pinned version).
3. Run `bun run build:local`.

The build fetches the dependencies it pins; it does not use a prebuilt WebKit.
Upstream pins its own toolchain versions in `scripts/build/ci-images/spec.ts`;
those pins are upstream's, not Debian's, and no claim is made here about
whether Debian ships them.

## What this package contains

- The official `bun` executable for each architecture, taken from the pinned
  GitHub release asset and verified against its published SHA-256 digest.
- A package-owned `bunx` relative symlink to `bun`. Upstream's own links in the
  release ZIP are not trusted or copied.
- `LICENSE.upstream.md`: upstream's `LICENSE.md` at tag `bun-v1.4.3`, byte for
  byte.
- `LGPL-2.0.txt` and `LGPL-2.1.txt`: the GNU LGPL texts that apply to the
  statically linked JavaScriptCore/WebKit and TinyCC sources.
- A `copyright` file recording this provenance and the licence texts.

No source archives are included in this package.